# Week 8 / MP2 — Custom Constellation Creator (Star Map)

Context for AI assistants working on **Mini Project 2** in `Week 8/`.  
Course: **HCDE 530**. Extends **`MP1/mp1b_visualizations.ipynb`** (HYG catalog, naked-eye filter, 2D sky vs 3D distance lesson).

**Project name:** TBD  
**Declaration:** **`Week 8/MP2a.md`** (final — source of truth)  
**Competency claims (`mp2.md`):** holistic across the project; details later.

---

## MP2a declaration (final)

### 1. Problem

People who want to creatively engage with the night sky have no tool that lets them invent **personal constellations** from imagination and see them mapped onto **real stars**. This tool lets anyone draw using **straight-line segments** on a sketch pad, have **each vertex snapped** to the nearest catalog star, and receive an **AI-generated name**.

### 2. Audience

- **Primary:** **General public**, **astronomy hobbyists**, **artists** — low-friction, playful, visually rich; no astronomical background required.  
- **Secondary:** Educators and science communicators (welcome, not primary framing). Built for **curiosity and creative expression** first.

### 3. Data

- **HYG v4.2**, `mag < 6.5` → **~9,000** naked-eye stars (~8,835 in MP1).  
- **Repo:** `prepare_stars.py` → **`stars_visible.csv`** (`id`, `ra`, `dec`, `mag`, `ci`, `spect`, `lum`, `proper`, `dist`, `x`, `y`, `z`).  
- **Client:** CSV loaded in browser.  
- **Names:** Optional **Supabase `used_names`** for global uniqueness only. **No** persistence of full constellation records (path, star sets, share DB).

### 4. Track

**Design track** — interface is the product: immersive galaxy map, straight-line sketch pad, snap-to-star on real stars, **2D/3D toggle**, **PNG export**. Vertex normalisation, nearest-neighbour snap, and Claude naming are **invisible infrastructure**.

### 5. Platform

- **Lovable** — React UI, deploy URL for MP2 submission.  
- **Claude API** — Lovable **edge function** for naming (keys in env only).  
- **Supabase** — **optional**, **`used_names` registry only**.

### 6. Rationale

Value = **look and feel** (galaxy aesthetic, **Roboto Mono**, draw-to-constellation, 2D/3D). Lovable ships the frontend fastest. **Nearest-neighbour snap** on ~9k stars runs **client-side in JavaScript** — no compute backend; Bolt not needed at this scale.

---

## What we are building

Deployed **creative constellation tool**: ~9k real stars; **sketch pad** (straight segments) → **vertex snap** → overlay on **2D map** (default, pan/zoom) + **3D toggle**; text description → **Claude** name; **PNG download**; optional global name check via Supabase.

**Must-have visuals:** `mag` → size; `ci` / `spect` → color; **distance** (especially 3D); **`proper` on hover** for **matched** stars only.

**Out of scope unless user asks:** full constellation DB, share-by-slug, accounts, 119k unfiltered HYG, classical-constellation editor.

